# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# THE FINAL ONE-BOX LIVE ENV — everything in one file, ready to copy.
#
# ONE box. ONE underlying. ONE lot per leg. Four legs submitted concurrently within each hedge
# wave. Under continuous human supervision.
#
# Every variable name below has been checked against the source, and every loader has been
# checked to see what a typo does. See §A.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── §A. WHAT A TYPO DOES — verified per variable, not assumed ────────────────────────────────
#
# These REFUSE TO BOOT on a malformed value, so a typo is loud and harmless:
#   BOX_MAX_OPEN_BOXES, BOX_SESSION_MAX_ENTRY_ATTEMPTS, BOX_SESSION_MAX_COMPLETED_TRADES,
#   BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY, BOX_LIVE_MAX_GROSS_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY,
#   BOX_LIVE_MAX_BOX_CAPITAL_RUPEES, BOX_ONE_ACTIVE_BOX_PER_UNDERLYING, BOX_ENABLE_SHORT_BOX
#
# ⚠ These SILENTLY FALL BACK, and their fallback is LOOSER than the value set here. A typo in one
#   of these weakens a limit without saying so:
#     BOX_LIVE_MAX_RESIDUAL_LEGS        typo → 1  (tolerates one residual leg; we ask for 0)
#     BOX_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_UNDERLYING typo → 2  (permits two per underlying; we ask for 1)
#     BOX_MAX_UNDERLYINGS               typo → 0  (NO CAP AT ALL; we ask for 1)
#     BOX_STRIKE_LEVEL                  typo → 3  (ATM ±3, a wider net; we ask for 1)
#
# These fall back in the SAFE direction (to off/false), so a typo cannot arm anything:
#   BOX_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED, ZERODHA_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED, BOX_SHADOW_MODE_ENABLED,
#   BOX_LIVE_ENTRY_SUBMIT_CONCURRENCY (garbage collapses to 1, the slow, safe width)
#
# SO: after applying this file, confirm what is actually in force. This is not optional — values
# can also be overridden by the shell, by PM2's env, or by an ecosystem file:
#
#     node dist/box/effectiveConfig.js
#
# Read back, at minimum: max_open_boxes, session ceilings, max_underlyings, strike_level,
# residual legs, per-underlying concurrency, and the leg-quantity caps.


# ── §B. YOUR EXISTING INFRASTRUCTURE — DO NOT COPY OVER THESE ────────────────────────────────
# Keep whatever the deployment already has; none of these belong in a committed file:
#   DATABASE_URL, MONGODB_URI, SESSION_SECRET, SITE_PASSCODE_HASH, CSRF_ALLOWED_ORIGIN,
#   BROKER_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY, ZERODHA_API_KEY / _SECRET, DHAN_* credentials,
#   CALSPREAD_DEPLOYMENT_ID, CALSPREAD_INSTANCE_ID, APP_TIMEZONE, DEFAULT_ACTIVE_BROKER
#
# ⚠ POSTGRESQL MUST BE CONNECTED. Without it the whole session-budget layer is INERT — both
#   session ceilings count nothing. Confirm `db_enabled: true` on /api/box/status before arming.
#
# ⚠ SET CALSPREAD_DEPLOYMENT_ID EXPLICITLY. Unset, the durable reservation lock namespace is
#   INFERRED, and two environments can then share one — a laptop could take a contract this
#   process needs. The engine warns about this at boot in live mode.


# ── §C. GO LIVE — three independent switches, all required ───────────────────────────────────
BOX_EXECUTION_MODE=live
BOX_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=true
ZERODHA_LIVE_TRADING_ENABLED=true

# Mutually exclusive with live; restated so a copy-paste cannot re-enable them and fail at boot.
BOX_SHADOW_MODE_ENABLED=false
BOX_PAPER_EXECUTION_PROFILE=standard


# ── §D. ONLY ONE BOX ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# BOX_MAX_OPEN_BOXES is the one that actually answers "I cannot fund a second box". It is the
# only global ceiling enforced in EVERY execution mode and decided BEFORE any exposure exists,
# and it counts committed exposure — open positions, unresolved partial entries, in-flight entry
# pipelines, confirmed-but-unrecorded fills, and reservations held over an uncertain outcome.
# At 1, a second box is refused on ANY underlying, in EITHER direction.
BOX_MAX_OPEN_BOXES=1

# Bounds what you TRY, not what you hold. An attempt that posted orders, partially filled and was
# unwound took real exposure and paid real charges, yet holds no inventory afterwards — so only
# this catches it. It is ALSO the only thing that refuses two entries admitted in the same
# instant. Do not raise it "to allow a retry": arm a fresh session instead.
BOX_SESSION_MAX_ENTRY_ATTEMPTS=1
BOX_SESSION_MAX_COMPLETED_TRADES=1

# Refuses a second box on the same underlying regardless of strike pair, expiry or direction.
# The code default is false — deliberately ON here.
BOX_ONE_ACTIVE_BOX_PER_UNDERLYING=true
BOX_MAX_CONCURRENT_PER_UNDERLYING=1

# ⚠ 0 does NOT mean unlimited here — the guard is `openBoxes >= limit`, so 0 means NO box may
#   ever open. Also note this one is LIVE-ONLY and is read from a count refreshed only after a
#   position exists, which is why BOX_MAX_OPEN_BOXES above exists.
BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_BOXES=1
BOX_LIVE_MAX_CONCURRENT_EXECUTIONS=1

# ⚠ the comparison is STRICTLY GREATER, so 0 tolerates no residual leg at all.
BOX_LIVE_MAX_RESIDUAL_LEGS=0


# ── §E. THE FOUR-LEG BURST ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4 = let both legs of a hedge wave travel together. It does NOT mean four simultaneous orders:
# entry is hedge-first in two waves (2 BUYs, then the 2 uncovered SELLs held until the hedges
# have attributed fill proof), and concurrency cannot overlap a SELL with its hedge. The gap
# between placements stays a real rate-limit wait — Zerodha 110 ms, hard floor 100 ms.
BOX_LIVE_ENTRY_SUBMIT_CONCURRENCY=4
BOX_LIVE_BROKER_ORDER_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=0
BOX_LIVE_BROKER_MIN_INTERVAL_MS=250


# ── §F. THE UNIVERSE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# BOX_MAX_UNDERLYINGS caps HOW MANY names are considered, chosen by the board's own priority
# order (indices first, then alphabetical) — you do NOT choose WHICH. At 1 you get NIFTY, which
# is why the quantity ceilings in §G are sized for a 75 lot.
#
# To choose BY NAME, use the operator blocklist — runtime, no restart:
#     GET    /api/box/excluded-underlyings
#     POST   /api/box/excluded-underlyings   {"symbol":"NYKAA","reason":"illiquid strikes"}
#     DELETE /api/box/excluded-underlyings/NYKAA
BOX_MAX_UNDERLYINGS=1
BOX_STRIKE_LEVEL=1
BOX_ENABLE_SHORT_BOX=false


# ── §G. «EDIT» QUANTITY AND CAPITAL — SIZED FOR NIFTY (LOT 75) ──────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠ THESE WILL REFUSE A SINGLE-STOCK BOX AS WRITTEN. That is deliberate, and there is a test
#   pinning it. A stock lot is far larger — PAYTM is 725 — so a per-leg cap of 75 refuses the
#   entry before the first order leaves. It looks exactly like "nothing ever qualifies".
#
# If you trade anything other than NIFTY, set all four from YOUR instrument:
#     BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY       = its one-lot quantity  (read it off the Box row)
#     BOX_LIVE_MAX_GROSS_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY = 4 x that
#     BOX_LIVE_MAX_BOX_CAPITAL_RUPEES      = above the box's GROSS ORDER NOTIONAL, not margin
#     BOX_LIVE_RECOVERY_RESERVE_RUPEES     = ~25% of that, held back for an unwind
#
# NIFTY 75 → 75 / 300. PAYTM 725 → 725 / 2900. Set the per-leg cap to the instrument's own lot;
# do NOT raise it globally "to be safe" — it is the barrier that stops a large stock lot being
# half-executed. Verify the current lot size rather than trusting these numbers: exchange lot
# sizes change, and 75 is only correct while NIFTY's is 75.
BOX_LIVE_MAX_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY=75
BOX_LIVE_MAX_GROSS_OPEN_LEG_QUANTITY=300
BOX_LIVE_MAX_BOX_CAPITAL_RUPEES=100000
BOX_LIVE_RECOVERY_RESERVE_RUPEES=25000


# ── §H. FUNDING ADMISSION — ALL ARMED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# With these on, MISSING or STALE broker evidence REFUSES the entry rather than assuming.
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_FUNDS_COVER=true
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_MARGIN_EVIDENCE=true
BOX_LIVE_REQUIRE_STAGE_FUNDING=true
BOX_LIVE_FUNDS_FRESHNESS_MAX_AGE_MS=5000
BOX_LIVE_MARGIN_FRESHNESS_MAX_AGE_MS=5000
BOX_LIVE_EVIDENCE_READ_TIMEOUT_MS=2500
BOX_LIVE_EVIDENCE_CONCURRENT_READS=false


# ── §I. FRESHNESS AND FOUR-LEG COHERENCE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BOX_QUOTE_MAX_AGE_MS=15000
BOX_FEED_MAX_AGE_MS=5000
BOX_MAX_CROSS_LEG_RECEIVE_DISPERSION_MS=500
BOX_MAX_CROSS_LEG_EXCHANGE_DISPERSION_MS=250
BOX_MAX_RECEIVE_TO_EXCHANGE_DELAY_MS=5000
BOX_COHERENCE_ZERO_DISPERSION_DISABLES_IN_LIVE=false


# ── §J. ECONOMICS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
BOX_MIN_EXPECTED_NET_PROFIT=1200
BOX_REQUIRE_PRICED_CHARGES=true


# ── §K. ORDER STREAM ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Off for a first supervised run: REST reconciliation is the proven path, and the stream adds a
# second moving part on the day you least want one.
ZERODHA_ORDER_STREAM_ENABLED=false


# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# §L. ON THE DAY — every step is a separate, deliberate action
#
#   1. Apply migrations. Confirm 012 applied.
#   2. Boot, then run:  node dist/box/effectiveConfig.js   and read back §A's list.
#   3. On /api/box/status confirm:
#        execution_mode "live" · db_enabled true · reconciliation_complete true
#        unknown_orders 0 · excluded_underlyings.readable true
#        risk.max_open_boxes_all_modes 1 · risk.box_inventory_held 0
#        operational_readiness.blockers — clear EVERY entry-scoped one
#   4. Confirm the broker session is the account you expect.
#   5. Set the blocklist for the day.
#   6. Arm in THIS order, so the panic button is live before anything can be sent:
#        live orders → emergency flatten → entry
#   7. Arm the session explicitly and CHECK the response:
#        POST /api/box/session/arm { "max_completed_trades": 1, "max_entry_attempts": 1 }
#      Confirm it reports max_entry_attempts 1 and remaining_entry_attempts 1. Both ceilings are
#      SNAPSHOTTED at arm time — editing this file and restarting does NOT rebind an already-armed
#      session. This is the most likely way to believe a bound is on while it is off.
#   8. RUN the scanner.
#
# ⚠ HAVE THESE OPEN IN A TERMINAL BEFORE YOU ARM. If the websocket drops while the box is open,
#   NO EXIT IS ATTEMPTED — the monitor requires a healthy feed, there is no REST fallback on the
#   exit path, and expiry-safety is checked after the same gate. Getting flat with a dead feed is
#   an operator action:
#        POST /api/box/live/cancel-working
#        POST /api/box/live/flatten
#   Both are independent of the entry controls. Reduction does NOT depend on the broker account
#   being nameable — verified, and covered by tests D2/P0-4/A3.
#
# §M. AFTER IT GOES FLAT — nothing stops by itself in this build:
#        POST /api/box/stop
#        POST /api/box/session/disarm
#        GET  /api/box/trades/history?scope=today     the numbers
#        GET  /api/box/events?limit=200               the decision trail
#        GET  /api/box/execution-attempts             anything attempted and aborted
#   `exit_charge_reconciliation` starts `pending`; fees read immediately after flat are LOCAL
#   estimates. Wait for it to settle before treating them as final.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
